WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.150
Hang a weight on a
spring, and it stretches.

2
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:06.010
Double the weight, and it
stretches twice as far.

3
00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:08.830
Take the weights off,
and it springs back.

4
00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:12.150
Keep adding weights, though,
and something changes.

5
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:14.890
One more weight, and when
you remove them all,

6
00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:17.290
the spring stays stretched for good.

7
00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:18.770
So what changed?

8
00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:22.110
In this mission, you'll use
Hooke's law to link force,

9
00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:24.050
extension and the spring constant.

10
00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:26.790
You'll find the limit of
proportionality on a graph,

11
00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:31.050
and tell elastic deformation
from inelastic deformation.

12
00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.300
Your mission: find out why the
spring stops springing back.
